  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Combating Trafficking in Persons Through Victim-Centered Approaches in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRS will work to increase government capacity to conduct victim-centered investigations and prosecutions of trafficking in persons cases as well as to provide comprehensive services to trafficking victims in four Indian states. Activities will include: capacity building for Indian law enforcement and legal professionals; advocacy for adoption of standard operating procedures for victim identification, referral, and protection; and the provision of services for trafficking victims, including the rehabilitation and creation of four shelters.</narrative>
  </description>
